# Shorebird OTA code-push — non-interactive credentials.
#
# Copy to .env.shorebird (gitignored by the `.env.*` rule) and fill in.
# NEVER commit the real file or paste the token into a log.
#
# WHY THIS EXISTS
# The Shorebird CLI stores an interactive login under
# ~/Library/Application Support/shorebird/credentials.json. That refresh token
# EXPIRES, and when it does every code-push deploy fails with:
#
#     Failed to refresh credentials.
#     Try logging out with shorebird logout and logging in again.
#
# which is a confusing way to be told a build cannot ship. It also cannot work
# in CI at all, because there is no browser to log in with. SHOREBIRD_TOKEN is
# the supported non-interactive path and takes precedence over the stored
# login, so setting it fixes both at once.
#
# HOW TO GET ONE
# Shorebird Console (account lazervault.sync@gmail.com, account 53396):
#   Account -> API Keys -> Create API Key
#   Name it, set an expiry, choose the permission level, copy the value.
# The value is shown ONCE. Set an expiry you will actually notice, and treat a
# rotation as a deploy-blocking task rather than a surprise.
#
# `shorebird login:ci` also mints a token if you prefer the CLI.
#
# CI: set the same value as the SHOREBIRD_TOKEN repository secret. The android
# and ios jobs run on different runners (ubuntu / macos-14), so BOTH need it.
SHOREBIRD_TOKEN=
